# 5. RESPONSIVE INTERACTION RULES

Use three principal layout ranges:

- Desktop: 992px and above.
- Tablet: 601px–991px.
- Mobile: 600px and below.

Follow the actual Figma breakpoints when available.

### Desktop

Enable the full cinematic experience where appropriate:

- Cursor-following imagery.
- Pinned product showcase.
- Scroll-triggered text reveals.
- Gentle 3D interactions.
- Editorial parallax.
- Section theme transitions.

### Tablet

Reduce animation complexity.

Avoid layouts requiring hover.

Use touch-friendly navigation and controls.

### Mobile

Prioritize readability, speed, and shopping usability.

- Disable cursor-following effects.
- Replace complex pinned stacks with accessible product layouts.
- Reduce parallax intensity.
- Preserve the mobile Figma compositions.
- Avoid horizontal overflow.
- Keep buttons and product selectors touch-friendly.
- Ensure cart and checkout work smoothly.

### Accessibility

Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

Disable decorative motion when requested.

Never hide essential content behind animations.

Support keyboard navigation, visible focus indicators, accessible labels, and sufficient color contrast.

